==English==

===Alternative spellings===
* [[palaeolithic]]

===Etymology===
From {{Gr.}} [[παλαιολιθικός]] (''paleolithikos''), from {{AGr.}} prefix [[παλαιο-]]
"[[paleo-]]", from [[παλαιός]] (''paleos'') "old" + λίθος (''lithos'') "stone".

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈpeɪl.ɪi.əʊˌlɪɵ.ɪk/}}, {{SAMPA|/"peIl.i:.@U.lIT.Ik/}}
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|/pălēōlĭthīk/}}, {{IPA|/ˈpæl.ɪi.oʊˌlɪɵ.ɪk/}}, {{SAMPA|/"p{l.i:.@U%lIT.Ik/}}
* {{hyphenation|PAH-lee-o-LITH-ik}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# A period that lasted from two and a half million years ago to 10,000 [[BC]]; the [[Old Stone Age]].

====Synonyms====
* [[Old Stone Age]]

